/E (Established in 1973 by an Act of the Indian Parliament, the North Eastern Hill University \(NEHU\) is a prominent institution in Shillong, India. It stands as a central institution for promoting education and research in the northeastern region of India. The dual-campus structure in Meghalaya, with locations in both Shillong and Tura, enables the university to cater to a broader base of students and researchers, fostering regional development and accessibility to education.  )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
endobj
